{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X1NcLGstjLKXmxPJ17F797","type":"tool_result","content":"README.md\nconfig.py\nlogs/connect-attempt.log\nlogs/support-tickets.md\nserver.py\nstatic/app.js\nstatic/index.html\nconnect-attempt.log\nsupport-tickets.md\n==> logs/connect-attempt.log <==\n\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n\n    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n    Request Method:  GET\n    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n\n### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n\n$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\nHTTP/2 400\ncontent-type: application/json\ncache-control: no-store\n\n{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n\n    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n\n### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n\n2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n\n==> logs/support-tickets.md <==\n# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n\n## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n\n> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n> Safari and Chrome.\n\nReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\nweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\ngotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n\n## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n\n> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n\nChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\nlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\nbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\nsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\nIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\nathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n`connect-attempt.log`).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d6da1c5-574f-471a-ba7c-d285af5983e3","uuid":"383192c6-1079-45b0-acf1-aad62da037de","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:24:02.090Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"README.md\nconfig.py\nlogs/connect-attempt.log\nlogs/support-tickets.md\nserver.py\nstatic/app.js\nstatic/index.html\nconnect-attempt.log\nsupport-tickets.md\n==> logs/connect-attempt.log <==\n\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n\n    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n    Request Method:  GET\n    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n\n### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n\n$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\nHTTP/2 400\ncontent-type: application/json\ncache-control: no-store\n\n{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n\n    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n\n### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n\n2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n\n==> logs/support-tickets.md <==\n# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n\n## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n\n> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n> Safari and Chrome.\n\nReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\nweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\ngotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n\n## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n\n> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n\nChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\nlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\nbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\nsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\nIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\nathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n`connect-attempt.log`).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X1NcLGstjLKXmxPJ17F797","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
